The quintessential American lunchbox and holiday cookie. Using creamy peanut butter combined with light brown sugar, a touch of milk, and butter-flavor shortening produces cookies that remain remarkably soft and chewy for days. Pressed with the nostalgic fork crisscross pattern for signature golden ridges.

*Adapted from [Allrecipes / Jif](https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/65354/jif-irresistible-peanut-butter-cookies/).*

## Ingredients

- 1 ¼ cups packed light brown sugar (approx. 275g)
- ¾ cup creamy peanut butter (approx. 192g)
- ½ cup butter-flavor shortening (or softened unsalted butter, approx. 96g)
- 3 tablespoons whole milk
- 1 tablespoon pure vanilla extract
- 1 large egg, room temperature
- 1 ¾ cups all-purpose flour (approx. 210g)
- ¾ teaspoon baking soda
- ¾ teaspoon fine sea salt

## Instructions

1. **Preheat and Prep:** Preheat your oven to 375°F (190°C). Position oven racks in the middle position. Line two large baking sheets with parchment paper or silicone baking mats.
2. **Cream the Peanut Butter Base:** In the bowl of an electric mixer fitted with the paddle (or using a hand mixer), combine the light brown sugar, creamy peanut butter, shortening or butter, milk, and pure vanilla extract. Beat on medium speed for about 2 minutes until completely smooth, pale, and fluffy.
3. **Blend in the Egg:** Add the egg and mix on medium-low speed just until fully integrated into the creamed batter, scraping down the sides of the bowl once.
4. **Add Dry Ingredients:** In a medium bowl, whisk together the all-purpose flour, baking soda, and fine sea salt. Add the dry ingredients to the mixing bowl in two installments, mixing on low speed just until streaks of dry flour vanish and a soft, pliable dough forms.
5. **Scoop and Stamp Crisscross:** Scoop rounded 1-tablespoon portions of dough (using a #60 cookie scoop or spoons) and place them onto the prepared baking sheets spaced 2 inches apart. Lightly dip the tines of a fork in flour (or granulated sugar for sparkle). Gently press the back of the fork into each dough ball to flatten slightly, then turn the fork 90 degrees and press again to create the iconic crisscross pattern.
6. **Bake to Soft Perfection:** Bake one sheet at a time at 375°F for 7 to 8 minutes. Watch closely: pull them from the oven the moment the edges just begin to show a hint of golden color and the tops look matte. Do not overbake; they will firm up as they cool while staying tender and chewy inside.
7. **Cool:** Let the cookies rest undisturbed on the warm baking sheet for 2 minutes to set their structure, then use a spatula to transfer them to wire cooling racks to cool completely.

## Notes

- **Shortening vs. Butter:** Butter-flavor shortening yields a taller, softer cookie that doesn't spread excessively and stays tender for days. If you prefer butter, use ½ cup of room-temperature unsalted butter and chill the shaped dough balls for 30 minutes before baking to prevent spreading.
- **Peanut Butter Selection:** Standard commercial creamy peanut butters (like Jif or Skippy) yield the best texture and structure. Natural peanut butters with separated oil can produce dry or greasy cookies.
- **Storage:** Keep stored in an airtight container with a piece of parchment between layers at room temperature for up to 1 week.
